    "problem": "The encoded-frame worker already limits receipt capture to one per16ms and one outstanding report. A second16ms filter used the main thread IPC delivery clock. Delivery can bunch after a main-thread stall; that second filter discards a correctly paced newer receipt.",
    "correction": "Remove only the redundant main-thread time filter. Keep worker pacing, one outstanding report, permission and transform checks, RTP integer/range/duplicate checks, channel readiness and1024-byte uplink buffering guard. The encoded frame is forwarded unchanged.",
    "server_worker_transport": "All three packaged core payloads are byte-identical127. No139/140 RTP or142/143 queue diagnostic hooks in the144 baseline runs.",
    "scope": "A concrete receipt correctness fix; no claim that this alone completes native queue or Mac performance qualification."
